What is it?

    RoT_Callers is a utility designed to display a given number of previous
    callers to your BBS.  How many and which callers are displayed is
    controlled via a configuration file.

How do I use it?

    Simply add the line:

                    \#3<path where you stored RoT_Callers>/RoT_Callers

    To your ENGLISH file (preferably at the "Session Complete" line - 1043
    in v0.977). Also, you need a copy of the RoT_Callers.config file in your
    DATA directory.  Information on how to edit the RoT_Callers.config file
    is included in that file.

    Install and configure the RoT_Callers.config file in your DATA directory.
    Options are described in the body of the config file.

    Lastly, RoT_Callers does not actually handle the displaying of the
    information. Instead, it creates a text file in your DATA dir
    called "RoT_Callers.data" which you can then display at any point
    in your system. (personally, I display it from my RoT_Logon program)

DISCLAIMER:  This software is old :-)  I originally wrote it when I was
             running C-Net and this is nothing more than a quick and
             dirty port... The next version will be a complete rewrite. :)

